## Frontier drought — keep the agent, swap the runtime

Canonical pins above stay. Do **not** rewrite `.cursor/agents/` frontmatter for a dry
pool. The next parent that follows this rule would just put Sol/Opus back.

**Standing flag:** `.cursor/rules/frontier-drought-flag.mdc` (`Status: ON` or `OFF`).
That file is always-on. If it says **ON**, do not spawn frontier models — not even
once “to check”. Matthew’s phrases and the usage-limit error are how the flag flips;
a lucky frontier spawn is **not** a refill.

**Drought is ON** when any of these is true:

- The standing flag is **ON**
- Matthew says “Drought is ON”, “frontier is dry”, “out of Other Models”, or
  “stop using Sol/Opus”
- A Task (or `@` spawn) fails with `Other Models usage limit reached`
- Cursor reports it switched off a frontier model because that pool is empty

Once ON, it stays ON for the rest of the conversation. Write-capable agents persist
it by setting the standing flag to **ON**. Readonly heads obey it and do not edit
the flag file.

**Drought is OFF** only when Matthew says “Drought is OFF”, “credits are back”, or
“frontier is back” (and a write-capable agent sets the standing flag to **OFF**).

